        {
          "page": 3,
          "title": "Evidence Inputs",
          "level": 2
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "2 Product Scope\n2.1 Decision Rights\nThe Scrum method uses product scope to make the next decision observable and reversible.\nTeams capture context, compare evidence, and assign a named owner for the next review.",
      "headings": [
        {
          "page": 4,
          "title": "Product Scope",
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "page": 4,
          "title": "Decision Rights",
          "level": 2
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "3 Sprint Mechanics\n3.1 Assurance Measures\nScrum records a measurable result for sprint mechanics and preserves the decision context.\nCheck Threshold\nTrace Evidence linked\nReview Owner assigned\nClose Action recorded\nSIGNAL\nCONTROL\nQUALITY\nFLOW",
      "headings": [
        {
          "page": 5,
          "title": "Sprint Mechanics",
